<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27119" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διο-γενής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sprung from Zeus,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> epith. of kings, <i>ordained and upheld by Zeus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.337
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. Ὀδυσεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.352
				</span></i>
			; later, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δ. θεοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					301
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				631
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1263
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διογενὲς κράτος,</span> of
			Pallas, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				127
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τέκνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					91
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμφίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					528
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἷμα τὸ δ.,</span> of Achilles,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				1195
			</span></i> (lyr.): generally, <i>divine,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Med.</u>
					1258
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			parox., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διογένης, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ους</span>, ὁ,</span> pr. n.
				[<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δῑ-</span> in 
				Ep.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ̆</span> in Trag.]</div>
